WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.072
The Tortoise and the Hare

00:00:02.772 --> 00:00:06.615
A Hare was making fun of the Tortoise one day for being so slow.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:10.399
"Do you ever get anywhere?" he asked with a mocking laugh.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:15.103
"Yes," replied the Tortoise, "and I get there sooner than you think.

00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:17.453
I'll run you a race and prove it."

00:00:18.103 --> 00:00:24.675
The Hare was much amused at the idea of running a race with the Tortoise, but for the fun of the thing he agreed.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:30.783
So the Fox, who had consented to act as judge, marked the distance and started the runners off.

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:34.366
The Fox waved his flag, and the race began!

00:00:34.716 --> 00:00:41.233
The Hare shot forward like a brown lightning bolt, while the Tortoise set one steady foot in front of the other.

00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:48.337
In no time at all, the Hare was so far ahead that the Tortoise was only a speck on the path behind him.

00:00:48.687 --> 00:00:50.341
The Hare laughed to himself.

00:00:50.691 --> 00:00:52.862
This race was already won, he thought.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:01:06.225
The Hare was soon far out of sight, and to make the Tortoise feel very deeply how ridiculous it was for him to try a race with a Hare, he lay down beside the course to take a nap until the Tortoise should catch up.

00:01:06.874 --> 00:01:12.422
The Hare curled up in the cool grass and was soon fast asleep, dreaming of his easy victory.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:20.227
The Tortoise meanwhile kept going slowly but steadily, and, after a time, passed the place where the Hare was sleeping.

00:01:20.876 --> 00:01:27.436
Step by step, never stopping, never hurrying, the Tortoise kept on toward the flower garland at the finish.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:34.710
But the Hare slept on very peacefully; and when at last he did wake up, he opened his eyes wide in shock.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.516
The Tortoise was gone!

00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:43.181
The Hare now ran his swiftest, stretching out in a desperate sprint with dust flying behind him.

00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:50.410
There, just ahead, the flower garland fluttered over the finish line, and the steady Tortoise was almost there.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:56.040
And then, to the great delight of the Fox, the Tortoise stepped across the finish line.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.801
He had won the race!

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.866
Moments later the Hare came panting up the path, too late.

00:02:02.216 --> 00:02:04.684
He could not overtake the Tortoise in time.

00:02:05.034 --> 00:02:08.010
He stared at the winner, and his long ears drooped.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.605
Slow and steady wins the race.

00:02:10.955 --> 00:02:16.864
And from that day on, the Hare never mocked the Tortoise again, and the two became the best of friends.
